<p>I strongly disagree.</p>
<p>For me, Rimple nailed what they were shooting for. Somewhere around -10 or -11 I settled into the groove of a fairly decent &quot;collection-of-odd-things&quot; SCP with a darkly whimsical vibe I rather liked, and around -15 I was really starting to get invested in them both as a group and as individuals. The interviews went on to paint some nice little character vignettes on top of that, and had me teetering on a &quot;yeah, okay. This is good creepy-cute, I can dig it.&quot; upvote. It brought my guard down- and then proceeded to veer into the best series of narrative whiplash curves I've read in months, ending on a strangely poignant and beautiful note. Don't trim a single piece- the whole is more than the sum of its parts in this case.</p>

							</div>

								
